# The repo-root .gitignore has a bare `coverage` rule for test-coverage OUTPUT
# (the top-level coverage/ run dir, *.out profiles). That pattern also matches
# this scenario's source directories that are legitimately named `coverage`
# (the readiness-scoreboard domain). Re-include the domain source — the
# coverage/ output dir and *.out profiles stay ignored via the root rule.
!api/handlers/coverage
!api/handlers/coverage/**
!api/internal/coverage
!api/internal/coverage/**
!cli/domains/coverage
!cli/domains/coverage/**
